cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Isotypic Bottleneck: A Representation-Theoretic Bound on Rank Collapse During Grokking, and Its Limits as a Precursor Signal"
authors:
  - family-names: Meherab
    given-names: "Md Muntaqim"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Daffodil International University"
date-released: 2026-08-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/isotypic-bottleneck"
abstract: >
  Effective-rank collapse has been proposed as an early, computationally
  cheap precursor to grokking, but it reliably precedes generalization on
  modular arithmetic while failing on sparse parity. This repository
  contains the representation-theoretic account of that asymmetry, the
  full experimental notebook (70 GPU runs, T4), every figure and result
  table reported in the paper, and the LaTeX source.
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: "The Isotypic Bottleneck: A Representation-Theoretic Bound on Rank Collapse During Grokking, and Its Limits as a Precursor Signal"
  authors:
    - family-names: Meherab
      given-names: "Md Muntaqim"
  year: 2026
  # NeurReps 2026 (NeurIPS workshop). Venue/proceedings details, and a DOI
